With stats like those, you should easily trash the Wiz, assuming a
couple of things:  You are fast, and have speed boots (this makes a
BIG difference!).  You have a ring of conflict handy in case he
summons a few friends to munch you.

Of course neither of these are necessary, but with intelligent
fighting they virtually assure victory.  Another handy thing to
have is an assortment of wands.  Wands of death are excellent, and a
wand of cancellation _should_ keep him from doing nasty things to you
(could be wrong there tho).  It's tough to hit the Wiz with a wand's
ray, but they're a nice ace up your sleeve...

Last game I played (won :) I had a very effective career as a wand
wielder, one zap once took out 2 (count em two) Wizards of Yendor, and
previously to that one zap took out both Orcus and Yeenghou (however ya
spell that)!  Of course wands of death are hard to come by and generally
aren't all that effective (and certainly can kill you as well, if you're
lacking certain intrinsics), but they do make a feasible last resort.

Also note the Wiz's habit of teleporting to the stairs to heal.  Corner
him there and either he retreats up the stairs or he's toast :)

